        "Harald Rose",
        "Knut Urban",
        "Maximilian Haider"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Aberration correction opened routine sub-angstrom electron microscopy and changed the ability to identify atomic structure in real materials.",
        "attribution": "Rose supplied foundational correction concepts; Haider and Urban were central to their practical realization and validation.",
        "maturity": "The achievement has long since become an indispensable, independently reproduced tool in materials science.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Electron-optical correction involved a wider technical community, complicating a three-person attribution."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 5,
      "ballot_id": "B013",
      "proposed_laureates": [
        "Henry J. Snaith",
        "Nam-Gyu Park",
        "Tsutomu Miyasaka"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Metal-halide perovskites revealed an unexpectedly powerful new photovoltaic platform with remarkable optoelectronic properties.",
        "attribution": "Miyasaka and Park pioneered the photovoltaic route, while Snaith drove the architecture that exposed its exceptional performance.",
        "maturity": "Independent progress has been extraordinary, although durable deployment remains less mature than the laboratory science.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Long-term stability, toxicity, and scalable manufacture remain unresolved for broad application.",
          "The discovery-to-device credit chain is unusually extensive."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 6,
      "ballot_id": "B012",
      "proposed_laureates": [
        "Kenji Watanabe",
        "Takashi Taniguchi",
        "Philip Kim"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Ultrapure hexagonal boron nitride made clean van der Waals heterostructures and many subsequent two-dimensional quantum discoveries possible.",
        "attribution": "Watanabe and Taniguchi produced the crucial materials; Kim was a leading force in establishing their use in high-quality heterostructures.",
        "maturity": "The material platform is well established and its influence across two-dimensional physics is unmistakable.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Its central importance is enabling rather than a discrete physical discovery.",
          "The proposed three-person allocation may omit other key heterostructure pioneers."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 7,
